repl_init_from_source — implementation plan
============================================

status: planned (2026-07-09)

references I1..I5 (plans/repl_list); builds on plans/repl_init.

this is the only wave-1 tool whose scala handler is more than a pass-
through: the client speaks (theory, offset | pattern | index), the
engine speaks either Ir.init_from_document node_name command_id (PIDE
document, use_theories-loaded theory) or Ir.init ["Thy:idx"] (recorded
segments, image theory). the scala side owns the resolution (spec:
"theory loading and checking" + implementation order item "command-
target resolution (offset/pattern -> command id)").

advertised metadata (the builtin table row)
-------------------------------------------

name          repl_init_from_source
description   "Create a new REPL proof session rooted at a specific
              command inside an existing theory, so you can step from
              the middle of a proof or after a definition instead of
              rebuilding context from imports. Give the theory's long
              name plus exactly one locator: `offset` (character
              offset into the source), `pattern` (a literal source
              substring; its first occurrence picks the command), or
              `index` (command/segment index). Works on theories
              loaded with load_theory (PIDE document) and on image
              theories with recorded segments. The REPL starts at the
              state AFTER the located command."
              (source: mcp_server.py init_from_document :307 +
              init_at_line :488, generalized to the spec's locator
              triple.)
inputSchema   {"type": "object",
               "properties": {
                 "repl": {"type": "string"},
                 "theory": {"type": "string"},
                 "offset": {"type": "integer"},
                 "pattern": {"type": "string"},
                 "index": {"type": "integer"}},
               "required": ["repl", "theory"]}
              (exactly one of offset/pattern/index; json schema
              oneOf-with-required is outside the common subset we
              committed to, so the constraint is enforced in the
              handler and stated in the description.)
annotations   {"readOnlyHint": false, "idempotentHint": false,
               "openWorldHint": false}
outputSchema  none.

name/argument mapping across the layers
---------------------------------------

  mcp client edge   tools/call "repl_init_from_source",
                    {"repl": "R", "theory": "Draft.Foo", "pattern": "lemma foo"}
  scala handler     1. resolve the theory name against the headless
                       session's snapshot (use_theories-loaded) or the
                       recorded-segments index (image theory).
                    2. resolve the locator to a command:
                       - snapshot: offset -> Command at offset;
                         pattern -> first command whose source contains
                         it; index -> nth command. -> command id.
                       - segments: offset/pattern -> containing/first-
                         matching segment; index used directly.
                    3. call backend.ir("init_from_document",
                       [(repl, R), (node_name, <node>), (command_id, <id>)])
                       or backend.ir("init",
                       [(repl, R), (theories, "<thy>:<idx>")]).
  ml dispatcher     "init_from_document" {repl, node_name, command_id}
                    (already in the dispatcher) or "init" (see
                    plans/repl_init).
  engine            ir.ML:426 init_from_document — Document.command_exec,
                    eval must be finished, base_state = eval result;
                    out "Created REPL <id> from document ... [proof|theory]".
                    or ir.ML:393 init with a segment spec.

implementation steps
--------------------

1. [infra, shared with goto_definition] snapshot access on
   MCP_Session: a way to get the Document.Snapshot for a loaded node
   and enumerate its commands (id, source, range). template:
   Headless session .current_state / snapshot APIs used by
   Server_Commands.
2. [this tool] the locator resolution function, PURE where possible:
   (commands: List[(id, offset, source)], locator) -> Either[error, id]
   so it unit-tests without a prover. errors: theory not loaded and
   not segment-recorded; pattern not found; offset/index out of range;
   zero or several locators given.
3. [this tool] builtin row + handler branching to the two fnames as in
   the mapping; engine errors -> isError results.
4. tests; rebuild per rules.

