    test [scala unit]: canned command list, all three locators, plus
    each error case (not found, out of range).
T3  Ir.init_from_document requires the command to be executed and
    finished; an unexecuted command is a status error, not a hang.
    test [bridge]: load a theory via the scala path, init_from_source
    at a command past the checked region guarded by the engine's
    "still being evaluated"/"has not been executed" errors.
T4  the segment fallback works for image theories with recorded
    segments (record_theories sessions, e.g. MCP-HOL's own theories),
    where no PIDE document exists.
    test [ml unit]: dispatch "init" with a "Thy:idx" spec against a
    recorded theory -> ok (shared with plans/repl_init T6).
T5  the created repl behaves like any other: visible in repl_list
    with origin "document ... cmd N" (or "Thy:idx"), steppable,
    removable.
    test [e2e]: load_theory a small fixture, repl_init_from_source at
    a lemma by pattern, repl_step "by simp" variant, repl_text,
    repl_remove.

open question (resolve while implementing, then fold into the spec):
whether the mid-proof attach uses the state BEFORE or AFTER the
located command — Ir.init_from_document gives AFTER (eval result);
attaching "at the failing command" (the spec's workflow step 3) needs
the command *before* the failing one. either the resolver picks the
predecessor when the intent is "attach at" or the description keeps
the AFTER semantics and the skill teaches pattern-on-predecessor.
plan assumes AFTER + description honesty.

